first names that format and the columns the guess rests on. With a full map as \code{col_map},
a file that no format fits is read by the map alone, and the attribute
\code{source} gives its format as \code{"col_map"}.

\strong{Time.} Every datetime is returned in UTC. OTN, GLATOS and VUE exports are
written in UTC. A header that states an offset, such as
\code{"Date and Time (UTC-04:00)"}, and a stamp that carries one, such as
\code{"2024-05-01T10:00:00-04:00"}, are read at that offset. In a VDAT file the
\code{Time} column is the receiver's corrected time at the \verb{Time Offset (h)} of
its row; where \code{Time} is blank the uncorrected \verb{Device Time (UTC)} is used.
\code{tz} reads stamps that carry no zone in another zone, for a file exported
in local time.

\strong{Sensors.} Readings with no unit, or the unit \code{"ADC"}, are raw counts.
They go to \code{sensor_raw} and leave \code{sensor_value} and \code{sensor_unit} as \code{NA}
until \code{\link[=calibrate_sensors]{calibrate_sensors()}} converts them. Readings with a physical unit go
