interrupted copy or sync leaves it, has that row dropped with a warning.
A last row cut short that still ends in a line end has its first fields
and NA in the rest. Rows at the end of a file with no \code{transmitter},
\code{receiver_serial} or \code{station_id} are dropped with one warning that
counts them, and \code{cut_rows} in the \code{source} record counts them too.
